children?</strong></p>"},"subContentId":"16eb6bde-5b72-4e96-8306-4f829c37ee21","metadata":{"contentType":"Multiple Choice","license":"U","title":"Multiple Choice","authors":[],"changes":[],"extraTitle":"Multiple Choice"}},"pause":true,"displayType":"button","buttonOnMobile":false,"adaptivity":{"correct":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>Top-tier execution!</strong></p>"},"wrong":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>Well! Everyone makes mistakes!</strong></p>"},"requireCompletion":false},"label":"<p>Choose the best answer</p>"},{"x":76.38585770405936,"y":19.40805434255216,"width":10,"height":10,"duration":{"from":302.096,"to":305},"libraryTitle":"Multiple Choice","action":{"library":"H5P.MultiChoice 1.16","params":{"media":{"disableImageZooming":false},"answers":[{"correct":false,"tipsAndFeedback":{"chosenFeedback":"<div><em><strong>Too simple.</strong></em><strong> While safety is a factor, the video emphasizes that \"low affordance\" is about the lack of open-ended design and single-use functionality, not just the absence of danger.</strong></div>","tip":"","notChosenFeedback":""},"text":"<div><strong>Because traditional equipment is too safe.</strong></div>"},{"correct":true,"tipsAndFeedback":{"chosenFeedback":"<div><em><strong>Exactly!</strong></em><strong> High-affordance environments allow children to \"fill in the possibilities.\" When a tool only does one thing, the child stops experimenting and starts following a pre-determined script.</strong></div>","notChosenFeedback":"","tip":""},"text":"<div><strong>Because low-affordance objects, like slides, have a single intended use which limits a child’s agency and problem-solving opportunities.</strong></div>"},{"correct":false,"tipsAndFeedback":{"chosenFeedback":"<div><em><strong>Incorrect.</strong></em><strong> The video actually cites a study (at 3:45) finding that children are often </strong><em><strong>more</strong></em><strong> likely to be seriously injured on traditional equipment, likely due to a decrease in environmental awareness and engagement.</strong></div>","tip":"","notChosenFeedback":""},"text":"<div><strong>Because children are statistically more likely to sustain serious injuries on adventure playgrounds due to the 'novelty' of the equipment.</strong></div>"},{"correct":false,"tipsAndFeedback":{"tip":"","chosenFeedback":"<div><em><strong>Partially true</strong></em><strong>, but varied terrain is primarily linked to \"motor control\" (1:07) rather than being the defining characteristic of low affordance.</strong></div>","notChosenFeedback":""},"text":"<div><strong>Because traditional playgrounds fail to provide the 'varied terrain' required to develop basic social skills.</strong></div>"}],"overallFeedback":[{"from":0,"to":50},{"from":51,"to":100,"feedback":"You're the best educator!"}],"behaviour":{"enableRetry":true,"enableSolutionsButton":true,"enableCheckButton":true,"type":"single","singlePoint":false,"randomAnswers":true,"showSolutionsRequiresInput":true,"confirmCheckDialog":false,"confirmRetryDialog":false,"autoCheck":false,"passPercentage":100,"showScorePoints":true},"UI":{"checkAnswerButton":"Check","submitAnswerButton":"Submit","showSolutionButton":"Show solution","tryAgainButton":"Retry","tipsLabel":"Show tip","scoreBarLabel":"You got :num out of :total points","tipAvailable":"Tip available","feedbackAvailable":"Feedback available","readFeedback":"Read feedback","wrongAnswer":"Wrong answer","correctAnswer":"Correct answer","shouldCheck":"Should have been checked","shouldNotCheck":"Should not have been checked","noInput":"Please answer before viewing the solution","a11yCheck":"Check the answers. The responses will be marked as correct, incorrect, or unanswered.","a11yShowSolution":"Show the solution. The task will be marked with its correct solution.","a11yRetry":"Retry the task. Reset all responses and start the task over again."},"confirmCheck":{"header":"Finish ?","body":"Are you sure you wish to finish ?","cancelLabel":"Cancel","confirmLabel":"Finish"},"confirmRetry":{"header":"Retry ?","body":"Are you sure you wish to retry ?","cancelLabel":"Cancel","confirmLabel":"Confirm"},"question":"<p><strong>According to play research and the concept of 'affordance,' why might a traditional plastic slide be considered a 'lower quality' developmental tool compared to a junk playground fire pit or building site?</strong></p>"},"subContentId":"39cdeb03-4294-49bf-85c4-3e7c72486b30","metadata":{"contentType":"Multiple Choice","license":"U","title":"Multiple Choice","authors":[],"changes":[],"extraTitle":"Multiple Choice"}},"pause":true,"displayType":"button","buttonOnMobile":false,"adaptivity":{"correct":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>Spot on!</strong></p>"},"wrong":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>Keep trying!</strong></p>"},"requireCompletion":false},"label":"<p>Choose the best answer</p>"},{"x":64.38236577913575,"y":11.644832605531295,"width":10,"height":10,"duration":{"from":239,"to":243},"libraryTitle":"Statements","action":{"library":"H5P.Summary 1.10","params":{"intro":"<p><strong>If you were to choose between digging a small trench and preparing a flower bed for your students, what would you choose and why?</strong></p>","summaries":[{"subContentId":"3b31757b-e63f-4885-828b-a54b8ff76e02","summary":["<p>Choosing the flower bed because the open-ended nature of the task allows children to shape their environment and manage the functional risks of using real tools.</p>","<p>Selecting the trench activity because it provides a clear, single-use goal that minimizes the risk of children using tools incorrectly.</p>","<p>Opting for the trench activity specifically to keep the children in a 'low-novelty' environment where they can repeat the same motor action safely.</p>","<p>Avoiding both activities until plastic, low-affordance replicas of tools can be sourced to ensure a zero-injury environment.</p>"],"tip":"<p><strong>This combines high affordance (open-ended design) with the \"freedom\" and \"agency\" required for children to develop better judgment and confidence.</strong></p>"}],"overallFeedback":[{"from":0,"to":0,"feedback":"This choice prioritizes \"single-use\" goals or \"low-novelty\" environments. Research suggests that for play to be most beneficial, children need high-affordance tasks and novelty to develop the judgment and confidence necessary to manage their own safety."},{"from":1,"to":100,"feedback":"The \"flower bed\" is superior pedagogically because it is high-affordance; it offers varied terrain and multiple ways to interact with the soil, unlike the more \"single-use\" nature of a trench."}],"solvedLabel":"Progress:","scoreLabel":"Wrong answers:","resultLabel":"Your result","labelCorrect":"Correct.","labelIncorrect":"Incorrect! Please try again.","alternativeIncorrectLabel":"Incorrect","labelCorrectAnswers":"Correct answers.","tipButtonLabel":"Show tip","scoreBarLabel":"You got :num out of :total points","progressText":"Progress :num of :total"},"subContentId":"cbf710f9-296f-424a-a76c-d6646ced45c3","metadata":{"contentType":"Summary","license":"U","title":"Reflection","authors":[],"changes":[],"extraTitle":"Reflection"}},"pause":true,"displayType":"button","buttonOnMobile":false,"adaptivity":{"correct":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>You’ve set a high bar with this!</strong></p>"},"wrong":{"allowOptOut":false,"message":"<p><strong>Oops!</strong></p>"}},"label":"<p>Choose the right situation</p>"}],"bookmarks":[{"time":16.133512,"label":"1"},{"time":42.553426,"label":"2"},{"time":56.982558,"label":"3"},{"time":78.578398,"label":"4"},{"time":100.313563,"label":"5"},{"time":114.904654,"label":"6"},{"time":162.895,"label":"7"},{"time":191.306115,"label":"8"},{"time":213.37031,"label":"9"},{"time":239,"label":"10"},{"time":302.097051,"label":"11"}],"endscreens":[{"time":324,"label":"5:24 Submit screen"}]},"summary":{"task":{"library":"H5P.Summary 1.10","params":{"intro":"<p>Choose the correct statement.</p>","summaries":[{"subContentId":"225c2335-8082-4d50-b4af-e94f9dd7a808","tip":"","summary":["<p>High-affordance environments maximize development by offering open-ended design, allowing children the agency to shape their surroundings and manage their own risk.</p>","<p>Low-affordance tools, like plastic sand scoops, are safer because they prevent children from experiencing the frustration that leads to accidents.</p>","<p>Adventure playgrounds with scrap materials are statistically more dangerous than traditional playgrounds because they lack fixed safety rules.</p>","<p>The primary benefit of 'risky play' is that it allows children to master adult tools early, reducing their need for adult supervision in the long term.</p>"]}],"overallFeedback":[{"from":0,"to":0,"feedback":"While these reflect common safety concerns, research shows that \"low-affordance\" designs often lead to disengagement, and traditional playgrounds can actually see higher injury rates because children become less mindful of their environment."},{"from":1,"to":100,"feedback":"Correct! High affordance (like a sandbox or a pile of scrap wood) allows for \"freedom and novelty,\" which are the key factors identified to maximize play's developmental benefits."}],"solvedLabel":"Progress:","scoreLabel":"Wrong answers:","resultLabel":"Your result","labelCorrect":"Correct.","labelIncorrect":"Incorrect! Please try again.","alternativeIncorrectLabel":"Incorrect","labelCorrectAnswers":"Correct answers.","tipButtonLabel":"Show tip","scoreBarLabel":"You got :num out of :total points","progressText":"Progress :num of :total"},"subContentId":"e8638bbf-288d-481a-ac1d-173e212c85a7","metadata":{"contentType":"Summary","license":"U","title":"Summary","authors":[],"changes":[],"extraTitle":"Summary"}},"displayAt":5}},"override":{"autoplay":false,"loop":false,"showBookmarksmenuOnLoad":false,"showRewind10":true,"deactivateSound":false,"showSolutionButton":"on","retryButton":"on","preventSkippingMode":"forward"},"l10n":{"interact